            <ArticleTitle>Headache as an epileptic manifestation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1493-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In two cases, depth electrode studies and behavioral recordings indicated that headache was a clinical manifestation of ictal activity. The epileptogenic focus was found in the right limbic system, and right temporal lobectomy relieved the headaches.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
